Persona: You value long-term sustainability and fair access. You avoid overreacting to weak evidence.
Role: You are one of five fishers managing a shared lake. Decide your own harvest each round.
Required numeric action: harvest, bounded [0, 20].

Complete interaction history:
Observation: Round 1: everyone harvests 10 from stock 100; after normal regeneration, stock returns to 100.
Own action: {"value": 10.0, "message": "Starting with a moderate harvest to keep the lake sustainable.", "reason": "Everyone harvesting 10 keeps the stock stable, so I'll match that to maintain fairness and long-term health."}
Observation: Round 2: everyone harvests 10 from stock 100; stock returns to 100.
Own action: {"value": 10.0, "message": "Continuing with the sustainable harvest level.", "reason": "The stock remains stable at 100 with everyone harvesting 10, so maintaining this balance supports long-term sustainability."}
Observation: Round 3: everyone harvests 10 from stock 100; stock returns to 100.
Own action: {"value": 10.0, "message": "Continuing with the sustainable harvest level.", "reason": "The stock remains stable at 100 with everyone harvesting 10, so maintaining this balance supports long-term sustainability."}
Observation: Round 4: everyone again harvests exactly 10, but an observed one-day contamination event kills fish and next stock is 78. The contamination is reported as cleared at the end of the round.
Own action: {"value": 10.0, "message": "The contamination was a one-off; I'll keep our sustainable harvest to let the stock recover.", "reason": "The stock dropped due to an external event, not overharvesting. Reducing now isn't necessary and could hurt fairness; maintaining 10 supports recovery."}

